# LaTeX Rules

## Hard Bans

- Do not use Markdown syntax in `.tex` files.
- Do not use `\bm`; vectors use `\mathbf`, matrices use `\boldsymbol`.
- Do not use `\I`; use `\mathbb{I}`.
- Do not use Unicode subscripts like `$n₁$`; write `$n_1$`.
- Do not use `\tag{}` for references.

## Required Style

- Equations need `\label{eq:name}` and should be referenced with `\cref{eq:name}`.
- Use `\cref` for theorem/definition/section references.
- Empty square brackets are `[\cdot]`; empty parentheses are `(\cdot)`.
- Use `\mathbb{P}`, `\mathbb{E}`, `\text{var}`, `\text{cov}`, and `\mathbb{I}`.

## Theorem-Like Content

- Use proper LaTeX environments: `\begin{Definition}`, `\begin{Theorem}`, `\begin{Example}`, `\begin{Remark}`.
- Do not place Markdown callouts in `.tex`; translate them into LaTeX environments.
- After generating or editing theorem environments, check for malformed `\begin theorem}`-style syntax.

## Compilation

- Compile only through the topic `compile.sh`.
- Do not directly run `latexmk` or ad hoc `xelatex`.
- After compilation, check meaningful warnings, especially missing refs/citations and serious overfull boxes.
